{"_meta":{"securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["people_table:read"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"description":"Read a job\u2019s People table: action=query returns one keyset page (people_table.rows.query) \u2014 search, a filter group over column ids, up to five sorts, projection, facets and an optional saved view; pass page.nextCursor back as cursor with the same query to continue. action=row returns one person\u2019s row by jobPersonId (people_table.rows.get); a missing, foreign or withheld person is a 404. strict (default true) refuses a non-queryable column; strict=false skips it and lists it in diagnostics, unless that would leave an OR group with no terms, which is refused either way. A malformed rule is INVALID_FILTER either way. Columns are addressed by id (country, custom:<fieldId>). Contact, financial and compliance columns are redacted for API keys and read exactly like unknown columns (COLUMN_NOT_QUERYABLE); Project To-do columns also need project_todos:read and Screening lms:read; candidate-written text (profile title, city, skills and other tag lists) is scrubbed of contact data and the surname and is selectable only. Names are the public \"First L.\" (else \"Unnamed candidate\") and selectable only: no search, filter, sort or facet runs on a name, and a query with no sort returns a stable order that is not by name. Address a person by jobPersonId. Banned, closed and non-visible candidates never appear in rows, counts or facets. Reads spend the key\u2019s budget (120 requests a minute and 50,000 rows an hour across jobs and surfaces); a spent budget is a 429 RATE_LIMITED with a retry delay. Requires people_table:read.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"action":{"enum":["query","row"],"type":"string"},"columns":{"description":"Projection by column id; default = the view or table defaults (query), every available column (row).","items":{"pattern":"^(?:[a